WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.067
-There was stunning news
in the worlds of politics

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.133
and media today
when Fox News announced

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.367
that they were abruptly
cutting ties

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:08.968
with their top rated host,
Tucker Carlson,

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.868
less than a week
after a massive settlement

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.300
over the Dominion Voting Systems
defamation lawsuit.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.033
For more on this,
it's time for a closer look.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:19.634
♪♪

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:22.133
We've been doing this show
for just over nine years.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:23.667
Eight of those
have been dominated

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.767
by the nonstop insanity
of the Trump era.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.067
So I didn't think anything
could shock me anymore.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.634
Then today, this happened.

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:32.367
-Big breaking news in media,
big business story,

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.100
big media story,
big political story.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.767
Fox News announcing in the
last hour Tucker Carlson is out

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.501
effective immediately.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.534
-Tucker Carlson is out
at Fox News?

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:45.000
Oh, my God, does this mean
Fox News has gone...

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.133
[Echoes] woke?
[ Thunder rumbles ]

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:52.267
[ Applause ]

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.767
When I heard that news,

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:57.200
I went through all the stages
of Tucker's face in one sitting.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.434
First, I was shocked...

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.534
...then I was confused...

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:04.834
...then I did the Tucker laugh.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.033
[ Laughs maniacally ]

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.300
That's actually
closer than you think.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:12.133
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.501
-But then I had
so many questions.

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.200
What are we gonna do
without Tucker?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.467
Who else is going to tell us
when M&amp;Ms are [Bleep] anymore,

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.100
you know?

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.534
You know, would be
really funny, though,

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.567
if they replaced him at 8 P.M.
with the new green M&amp;M.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.968
That'd be pretty funny.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.501
The decision was apparently
so sudden

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:30.501
that according to
"The New York Times"...

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.601
And the announcement
from Fox was so stunning,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:41.267
even the network's own anchors
seemed caught off guard

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.634
when they read the official
statement on the air today

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.200
in what felt like a decree
from state television

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.100
in some sort of weird
cult-like dictatorship.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:52.367
-We have some news
from within our Fox family.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.000
Fox News Media
and Tucker Carlson

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.767
have mutually agreed
to part ways.

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:01.234
Tucker's last show
was this past Friday,

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.901
and starting tonight,
"Fox News Tonight" will air

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.701
live at 8 P.M. Eastern.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:09.467
It will be an interim show with
rotating Fox News personalities

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.667
until a new host is named.

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:13.934
We want to thank Tucker Carlson
for his service

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:18.067
to the network as a host
and, prior to that,

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.934
as a long term contributor.

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.734
-Wow. I've seen more
convincing reads

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:26.200
on North Korean state TV.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.067
Tucker didn't even get
a farewell show.

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.234
Fox really knows
how to disappear someone.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.167
I'm shocked they didn't just go
with this as their statement --

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:49.367
So you heard there Tucker's last
show was Friday, April 21st,

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.334
which means -- and this
is totally real --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.934
that what I'm about to show you
is his final segment

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.133
as a Fox News anchor.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:56.501
-We'll be back.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:58.667
By the way, the entire
episode of "Let Them Eat Bugs,"

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:01.267
not quite as good as pizza,
streaming now on Fox Nation.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:04.033
Use a promo code "Originals"
for 30 days free.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.167
And we'll be back on Monday.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.701
-No, you won't.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.901
Turns out even that was a lie.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.901
Truly amazing, though,
his last segment on TV

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.000
was not a rousing monologue
or a grand farewell,

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.834
but a reminder to watch
a special report,

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.400
I guess, about eating bugs,

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.467
which apparently
is a problem now.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:23.934
That sounds like
how you get fired.

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:25.434
Rupert Murdoch calls you up
and says,

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:26.667
[ Australian accent ]
"Oi, Tucker, eat bugs,

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.133
you [ Bleep ]."

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.167
[ Normal voice ] And this is all
such a fitting end for Tucker,

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.400
because he was always terrified
that he'd lose his show

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.667
after getting canned at to other
cable networks, CNN and MSNBC.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.701
And he was specifically afraid
that Donald Trump

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:39.968
would be the one
to destroy him.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.534
Which is why Tucker spent
so much time spoon-feeding

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:43.901
Trump's bull[Bleep]
to his viewers

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.767
despite knowing it
was all bull[Bleep].

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.467
After the coup attempt
on January 6th,

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:48.467
Tucker called Trump --

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.467
Tucker made the same mistake

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.434
everyone else who sucks up
to Trump makes.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.334
He thought he could
harness Trumpism

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:58.868
and use Trump for his own ends

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.868
while remaining
completely unscathed.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.601
But ultimately, they all
learned the same lesson.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.400
You can't let a tiger loose
and not get mauled,

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:06.834
even if it's the biggest,

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:10.501
dumbest looking tiger
in the zoo.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:13.267
Ultimately -- Tiger's
not gonna catch me.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.367
Whoa!

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:16.934
Ultimately, Tucker's
shtick caught up to him.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.200
His whole game was framing

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.834
racist, conspiratorial
bull[Bleep]

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.501
and in a
"just asking questions"-style,

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.067
not taking responsibility
for anything,

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.734
but rather posing a bunch
of ludicrous hypotheticals

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.367
to scare his audience
like this one.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.968
-Curt Schilling wrote
a social media post

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.133
defending Donald Trump.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.467
And in 2021, that's not allowed.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:35.033
You could lose
your insurance for that.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.400
You could also lose
your bank account, your website,

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.267
your access to e-mail
and social media,

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.033
your ability to communicate
with the outside world.

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.167
And there's nothing
you can do about it,

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.534
because you can also
lose your lawyer.

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:47.834
No legal representation
for you.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.634
How long before they cut off
your water and electricity,

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:53.200
before UPS won't deliver
your packages.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.801
And not to wreck your day,
but guess what?

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:58.501
Amazon is now one of America's
biggest grocery providers.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.367
Good thing you
don't need to eat.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.934
-How long before they cut off
your water and electricity,

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.901
before UPS won't deliver
your packages?

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:07.234
How long until they cancel
your favorite TV show

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:08.767
and fire your favorite
TV show host?

00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:10.434
And what if that TV show host

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:13.234
is a person named
Tucker Carlson?

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:16.000
And what if it turns out
that you are Tucker Carlson

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.067
and you realize mid-monologue

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.067
that you're talking
about yourself?

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:20.367
What happens to you, then?

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:21.968
Do you go to CNN or MSNBC?

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.133
Because if you can't,

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.467
because those networks
already fired you,

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:25.767
what if you have
to go to Newsmax

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:27.200
and share a dressing room
with Mike Lindell

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.100
and he uses pillows
even though they're filled

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.901
with bricks and smell
like urine?

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.968
What if Newsmax refuses
to hire you

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:35.868
and Amazon refuses to deliver
packages and grocery stores

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.234
refuse to sell you food
in order to survive?

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.934
You have no choice but to...

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:40.968
-Eat bugs.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:41.968
-Now --

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:44.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.067
As we mentioned --

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:47.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.400
Tucker's abrupt ouster

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.501
comes less than a week
after Fox agreed

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:54.801
to pay a whopping $787 million
in the defamation case

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.634
brought by
Dominion Voting Systems

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.534
for pushing Trump's
deranged election lies.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.801
And they did that
because they were terrified

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:02.133
of losing Trump's audience.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.501
Now, personally, I would have
loved to see a trial,

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:05.834
mainly because it would
have been so funny

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.934
and cathartic to see Fox hosts
like Tucker

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.133
or Jeanine Pirro on the stand.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.267
"The election wasn't rigged.
I was just lying for ratings."

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:14.501
"Objection, Your Honor.

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.167
The Bible the witness
swore in on

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:20.667
is actually a box of wine with
Bible written on it in Sharpie."

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:22.000
But that would have been
bad for Fox,

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.000
and Fox knew that.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.033
Rupert Murdoch himself

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:25.367
would have been forced
to testify.

00:06:25.367 --> 00:06:26.901
And based on how
the deposition went,

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.000
Murdoch knew that
would not go well.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:39.667
He pointed a finger
at the lawyer

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:41.667
who had questioned him
for Dominion and said,

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.634
"I think he would
strongly disagree with that."

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:45.300
To which the Dominion lawyer
replied,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.000
"Indeed, I do."

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.467
Yeah, I would guess
the last thing a Fox employee

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:52.701
wants to see pointing their way
is Rupert Murdoch's finger,

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:55.767
a.k.a. the Reaper's scythe.

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:57.234
That's probably
how Tucker got fired.

00:06:57.234 --> 00:06:58.667
Rupert just pointed
a finger at him

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.734
and Tucker said,
"I'll get my stuff."

00:07:01.734 --> 00:07:03.934
Rupert Murdoch has never used
that bony appendage

00:07:03.934 --> 00:07:05.667
for the purposes
of delivering good news.

00:07:05.667 --> 00:07:08.067
[ Australian accent ] "Oi, you
there? That's right. You.

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:09.734
You know what
you're about to get?

00:07:09.734 --> 00:07:12.501
An edible arrangement

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:15.467
that says, 'Thanks
for all the hard work.'

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.100
Did you put the beetles
in the honeydew?

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.167
Oh, good, good. Very good.

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:22.100
Eat bugs, you [Bleep]."

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.701
[ Normal voice ] So --

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:29.634
So this case exposed
the grimy inner workings

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.400
of the right's leading
propaganda network,

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.334
like the fact that
they all thought Trump sucked

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:35.167
and thought his cronies
were morons and weirdos.

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:38.167
As you'll recall, one court
filing in the case revealed

00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:39.200
that Tucker had said of Trump...

00:07:44.434 --> 00:07:45.767
Among other things.

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:47.534
It's so funny to me that Tucker

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:49.601
talks like a divorcée
from a soap opera.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.267
"I'm so glad Aleister died
in that skiing accident.

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:53.934
I hate him passionately."

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:59.033
"Hello, darling, it's me.
I'm back from the dead.

00:07:59.033 --> 00:08:00.667
And now I'm...

00:08:00.667 --> 00:08:03.234
[Echoes] woke."
[ Thunder rumbles ]

00:08:03.234 --> 00:08:05.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:12.734
[ Applause ]

00:08:12.734 --> 00:08:14.634
But no matter how much
they hated him privately,

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:17.000
Tucker and his buddies
know they have to keep

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.300
Trump's base on their side,

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.267
which is why they kept
pretending to buddy up to Trump,

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:23.267
which is why he was so poetic
that one of Tucker's last acts

00:08:23.267 --> 00:08:25.767
as a Fox host
was flying down to Florida

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:27.400
to grovel in an interview
with Trump,

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:29.100
where he pretended
to be fascinated

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.767
by every word Trump uttered.

00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:32.367
Watch Tucker's
facial expressions

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:33.901
in each of these exchanges
with Trump.

00:08:33.901 --> 00:08:36.501
-I said, "Abdul,
if you do anything,

00:08:36.501 --> 00:08:38.200
you're gonna get
hit really hard."

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.801
Literally, I even -- he said,

00:08:40.801 --> 00:08:42.300
"But sir, why? Why?"

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.968
I wouldn't say it was
a long preparation,

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:45.501
but I did want to talk
about nuclear,

00:08:45.501 --> 00:08:47.868
because I consider it to be
the single greatest threat

00:08:47.868 --> 00:08:48.901
the world has.

00:08:48.901 --> 00:08:52.200
A beautiful female interpreter.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:53.367
She was very beautiful.

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:54.834
Today, if you say it,

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.734
they'll say, "This is terrible.
You're not allowed to say that."

00:08:57.734 --> 00:08:58.801
But she was very professional.

00:08:58.801 --> 00:09:00.868
She spoke every word for him.

00:09:00.868 --> 00:09:07.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:10.400
-He looks like a 12 year old
listening to his older brother

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.801
talking about touching a female
breast for the first time.

00:09:13.801 --> 00:09:15.701
"Yeah, it was over the sweater,

00:09:15.701 --> 00:09:17.567
but still it definitely
counted."

00:09:17.567 --> 00:09:20.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:20.033 --> 00:09:22.534
"That's so cool.
You're my idol."

00:09:22.534 --> 00:09:24.767
You can see it dawning
on Tucker's in real time.

00:09:24.767 --> 00:09:26.667
That's the moment
he thought to himself,

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:29.334
"Oh, I'm gonna get fired."

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:31.100
In fact, Tucker's prophecy

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.167
that Trump was a destroyer
seems to be coming true,

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:35.200
because as Tucker
loses his job,

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.767
Trump is ascendant in the polls
over his likely main rival,

00:09:37.767 --> 00:09:38.934
Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis.

00:09:38.934 --> 00:09:41.267
DeSantis has been
sinking in the polls,

00:09:41.267 --> 00:09:43.133
and instead of getting
tougher in response,

00:09:43.133 --> 00:09:44.968
he seems to be
getting more nervous

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:46.467
and looking pretty shaky.

00:09:46.467 --> 00:09:49.100
-What will Ron DeSantis do?
He is trailing in the polls,

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:53.200
struggling with endorsements,
and Trump clearly smells blood.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.868
-According to a new
"Wall Street Journal" poll

00:09:54.868 --> 00:09:58.467
taken last week, Trump pulled
in 48% of the support

00:09:58.467 --> 00:10:00.767
among likely Republican
primary voters.

00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:03.000
The next person closest
to him is DeSantis,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.067
who is 24 points behind.

00:10:06.067 --> 00:10:08.467
-Governor, polls show
you falling behind Trump.

00:10:08.467 --> 00:10:10.367
Any thoughts on that?

00:10:10.367 --> 00:10:11.868
-I'm not a candidate.

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:14.667
So we'll see if
and when that changes.

00:10:17.567 --> 00:10:20.234
-Holy -- Holy [Bleep],
look at his face.

00:10:20.234 --> 00:10:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.734 --> 00:10:25.167
He's acting like his mom just
found weed in his sock drawer.

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.634
"Ronald, is this your marijuana?

00:10:26.634 --> 00:10:27.934
That would certainly explain

00:10:27.934 --> 00:10:30.934
why you've been eating
pudding with your hands."

00:10:30.934 --> 00:10:33.501
Guys, there was a story
about Ron DeSantis

00:10:33.501 --> 00:10:34.634
eating pudding with his hands.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:35.934
And we know it wasn't
a big story,

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:37.334
but we're going to talk
about it a lot on the show

00:10:37.334 --> 00:10:38.334
over the next few months.

00:10:38.334 --> 00:10:40.100
We'd love if you caught up.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:43.767
Guy who ate pudding
with his hands

00:10:43.767 --> 00:10:45.467
thinks he should be president.

00:10:45.467 --> 00:10:46.767
Was just sitting there one day

00:10:46.767 --> 00:10:48.534
and was like, "You know,
who would make a good president?

00:10:48.534 --> 00:10:50.133
I think I would."

00:10:50.133 --> 00:10:52.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:52.934 --> 00:10:56.234
This dude is supposed to be
the great Republican savior.

00:10:56.234 --> 00:10:58.300
He's stammering
more than Cousin Greg.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.934
"Uh, I am not, uh,

00:10:59.934 --> 00:11:02.934
as of this hereby moment, uh,
a candidate as such.

00:11:02.934 --> 00:11:05.367
And, um, we shall see, uh,
if and when,

00:11:05.367 --> 00:11:07.501
upon consideration
of various, uh, factors,

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:12.634
if that should change
in any, uh, ch-- forthwith."

00:11:12.634 --> 00:11:14.234
It is too bad
we won't get another

00:11:14.234 --> 00:11:15.567
Tucker-DeSantis interview.

00:11:15.567 --> 00:11:17.968
They could have just made
these faces back and forth

00:11:17.968 --> 00:11:20.701
with each other.

00:11:20.701 --> 00:11:22.901
Tucker's ouster is obviously
a stunning development

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:24.300
in the world of politics
and media.

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:26.834
But it was yet again another
illustration of the core problem

00:11:26.834 --> 00:11:28.100
at the heart of GOP politics.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.934
They all try to suck up to Trump
and harness Trumpism

00:11:29.934 --> 00:11:31.467
for profit or political gain,

00:11:31.467 --> 00:11:32.968
and in the end,
they all get burned.

00:11:32.968 --> 00:11:35.234
In Tucker's case, he debased
himself in service of Trump,

00:11:35.234 --> 00:11:36.267
and it didn't work.

00:11:36.267 --> 00:11:37.601
All he'll ever be remembered for

00:11:37.601 --> 00:11:38.934
is devoting an entire segment

00:11:38.934 --> 00:11:41.334
to a piece of candy
of which Tucker said...

00:11:41.334 --> 00:11:43.133
-She's very beautiful.

00:11:43.133 --> 00:11:45.667
-This has been a closer look.

00:11:45.667 --> 00:11:49.634
♪♪

